  "Question": "Calculate \\((3+i)(3-i)\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "10",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Method 1: Conjugate product and modulus\n\nThe factors \\(3+i\\) and \\(3-i\\) are conjugates, so their product equals \\(|3+i|^2\\). The square of the modulus is \\(9+1=10\\).\n\nMethod 2: Difference of squares\n\nThe factors have the same real term and opposite imaginary terms, so the difference of squares formula applies. Using \\(i^2=-1\\),\n\\[\n(3+i)(3-i)=3^2-i^2=9+1=10.\n\\]",
